","Let $s_d$ is the number of steps per minute for D (David) and $d_d$ is the distance of each step for D.
$s_d = 80 \text{ steps/minute}$
$d_d = 65 \text{ cm/step}$
The speed of D is $v_d = s_d \cdot d_d = 80 \text{ steps/minute} \times 65 \text{ cm/step} = 520 \text{ cm/min}$.
The time taken by D to travel is $t_d = 20 \text{ minutes}$.
The distance from D to the first'd, let it be $d$, is $d = v_d \times t_d = 520 \text{ cm/min} \times 20 \text{ minutes} = 10200 \text{ cm}$.

Now, let $s_l$ is the number of steps per minute for L (D's) and $d_l$ is the distance of each step for D.
$s_l = 90 \text{ steps/min}$
$d_l = 55 \text{ cm/step}$
