* $f(a)$ is the y-coordinate of the point, which is the value of $f(a)$.

* $f'(a)$ is the derivative of $f$ evaluated at $0$ (the slope of the tangent line at the point (a, f(a))).
* $t$ is the variable of the equation of the line.

**Explanation:**

*   **The derivative (f'(a)) represents the slope of the tangent line:**  The derivative of a function at a point gives the instantaneous rate of change of the function at this point. This is equal to the slope of the tangent line tangent to the tangent line at this point.
