B = (N/2π) * (I/R)

Where:
*   B is the magnetic field strength (in Tesla)
* N is the number of turns of the coil
* I is the current (in Am)

* R is the radius of the coil (in meters)

Pl:
*   N = 100
*   I = 1 A
*   R = 0.2 m

Pl:
